  "captions": [
    {
      "start": 3,
      "end": 6.4,
      "text": "High above a sleepy meadow, the stars woke up one by one."
    },
    {
      "start": 6.5,
      "end": 9.8,
      "text": "The smallest star stretched, and yawned, and wobbled…"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.2,
      "end": 14.8,
      "text": "…and tumbled all the way down — plink! — into the clover, right next to Pip the snail."
    },
    {
      "start": 15,
      "end": 19.8,
      "text": "“Oh no,” she whispered. “I can't shine from down here.”"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.3,
      "end": 24.6,
      "text": "Pip was small, and Pip was slow, but Pip had a very big heart."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.8,
      "end": 28.8,
      "text": "“Hop on,” he smiled. “I'll take you home.”"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.3,
      "end": 33.8,
      "text": "Up the tallest hill they went, one tiny step at a time."
    },
    {
      "start": 34,
      "end": 38.8,
      "text": "But at the very top, the sky was still so far away."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.3,
      "end": 43.8,
      "text": "So Pip called out to his friends, the fireflies."
    },
    {
      "start": 44,
      "end": 48.8,
      "text": "Glow by glow, they gathered round and lifted the little star higher… and higher…"
    },
    {
      "start": 49.2,
      "end": 53.5,
      "text": "…all the way home. That night she shone brighter than ever,"
    },
    {
      "start": 53.7,
      "end": 58,
      "text": "and every night after, she twinkled a little extra — just for Pip."
    }
  ],
